{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>On the very essence of this day</b>. The commentators said that its meaning is in the body of this day itself, and likewise 'And bread and parched grain and fresh ears you shall not eat until the very essence of this day' (Leviticus 23:14) — until the body of the day, and likewise 'and like the very essence of the heavens for clarity' (Exodus 24:10) — the body of the heavens. And we cannot explain that it alludes to the essence of this day and its power, as our Sages said (Sifrei Ha'azinu §337) concerning the verses 'On the very essence of this day Noah came' (Genesis 7:13), 'On the very essence of this day HaShem brought out the children of Israel' (Exodus 12:51) — for it is written (Leviticus 23:32) 'On the ninth of the month at evening, from evening to evening,' and likewise 'And you shall call on the very essence of this day a holy convocation' (Leviticus 23:21) — the night too is included. Now He did not mention 'on the very essence of this day' regarding Sabbath or the other festivals, but only regarding the festival of Weeks (Leviticus 23:21) and Yom HaKippurim (here), and likewise regarding the prohibition of the new grain He said (Leviticus 23:14) 'until the very essence of this day.'\n\nAnd the apparent reason for the matter is this: because regarding Weeks He said 'From the day you bring the omer of the wave-offering… you shall count fifty days,' and He said 'And you shall bring a new meal-offering from your dwellings' and completed the subject (Leviticus 23:15–17), and He proceeded at length to command concerning the offerings (Leviticus 23:18–20), it was necessary to say (Leviticus 23:21) 'And you shall call on the very essence of this day a holy convocation' — for the body of the day itself is holy and forbidden in melakhah, and it is not dependent on the omer or on the offerings. And likewise regarding Yom HaKippurim, because He said (Leviticus 23:27) 'And you shall afflict your souls and bring a fire-offering to HaShem,' and in the section of Acharei Mot He further suspended the atonement on the offerings and on the scapegoat, therefore it was necessary to say (here): 'And all melakhah you shall not do on the body of this day, for it is Yom Kippurim' — in its own body it atones upon you, apart from the atonement of the offerings. And likewise 'until the very essence of this day' regarding the new grain (Leviticus 23:14) — until the body of this day, which is the day you bring the offering of your Elohim: even if the offering is not brought, the commandment applies in the body of this day, that the new grain is forbidden before it and permitted after it. And this is the reason He said (Leviticus 23:14) 'A perpetual statute throughout your generations in all your dwellings,' as I explained (Ramban on Leviticus 23:16).\n\nWe further find that Scripture mentioned 'on the very essence of this day' in matters decreed for appointed times. He said regarding Noah, 'On the very essence of this day Noah came' etc.; 'And it came to pass on the very essence of this day all the hosts of HaShem went out from the land of Egypt' (Exodus 12:41); 'And HaShem spoke to Moses on the very essence of this day: Ascend Mount Avarim' (Deuteronomy 32:48–49). And the reason in these is that it is possible Noah had brought into the ark beforehand many of the animals and birds; and likewise it is possible that some of Israel had gone out from Egypt beforehand, and on that day the matter was completed; and likewise before that day there had been a command to Moses our master regarding that ascent, and on that day he ascended. Therefore Scripture specified in all of them that they were in the body of that day — not that the matter began with them from the start and was completed on that day, but rather everything was on the very essence of this day. And likewise 'On the very essence of this day Abraham was circumcised' etc. (Genesis 17:26) — for they circumcised a great multitude on a single day, to declare his zeal in the commandments.\n\nAnd it further appears to me that the 'essence' of anything is its power and its strength, derived from the expression 'the power of my hand and the might of my arm' (Deuteronomy 8:17), 'might and strength' (Psalms 68:35), and likewise 'This one dies in the essence of his completeness' (Job 21:23) — in the strength of his completeness. And because bones are the foundation of the body and its strength, they are so called. And so 'like the very essence of the heavens for clarity' (Exodus 24:10) — that the clarity of the thing they saw was clear and strong like the strength of the clarity of the heavens. And therefore regarding the days mentioned He speaks of 'the essence of the day,' for the matter depends on them in and of themselves, not on any other thing added to them, namely the offerings that they would bring on them.\n\nAnd so Onkelos rendered (Onkelos on Leviticus 23:28) 'בִּקְרַן יוֹמָא הָדֵין' — in the horn of that day, in its body and its power, from the expression 'And all the horns of the wicked I will cut off' (Psalms 75:11), 'My shield and the horn of my salvation' (Psalms 18:3), for because strength is in the horns, the body of a thing is called its horn. And in the language of the Sages (Terumot 7:1): he repays the keren and does not repay the fifth. And there are those who have the reading in the Targum 'בִּכְרַן' with a kaph, and it is all one, for in Scripture 'כּוֹבַע' and 'קוֹבַע' are equivalent, and the Sages use every root of hindrance with a kaph, derived from 'and He does not restrain them when His voice is heard' (Job 37:4), and they say 'מִתְקַשֵּׁט' (Tosefta Ketubot 7:3) from תַּכְשִׁיטִין, and they said 'the ants gnawed it' (Pe'ah 2:7) from 'the boar from the forest gnaws it' (Psalms 80:14).\n\nAnd what is said in the aforementioned places, 'on the very essence of this day,' also means by the power of that day — for they are matters that would not be done in a single day according to the way of the world. Therefore He said that all the living creatures and all the beasts and all the birds and everything that creeps on the earth were gathered by the power of that day, by the decree of the El upon them, for His mouth commanded and His spirit gathered them. And likewise six hundred thousand footmen, apart from children, would not assemble and go out as one man from the land of Egypt, except by the power of the day decreed upon them so by the mouth of the Most High. And likewise regarding Moses our master, to declare that on the day he was commanded in the song and wrote it and taught it to Israel (Deuteronomy 31:22), and finished speaking all these words (Deuteronomy 32:45), it was decreed upon him that he would ascend by the power of that day in which the decree resided, to Mount Avarim, and he said 'And this is the blessing' and ascended there. And it is a matter fit for many days, but it was accomplished in the power and might of that day. And likewise the circumcision of three hundred and eighteen men on a single day in the house of Abraham — it was from HaShem.\n\nAnd Ezekiel said (Ezekiel 2:3), 'They and their fathers have rebelled against Me until the very essence of this day' — to include that day in the same category. And likewise 'until the very essence of this day' of the new grain — it is 'until' and 'until' inclusive, for the body of the thing is its power and its strength.\n\nAnd our Sages expounded (Sifra, Emor 14:7–8) from the expression 'on the very essence of this day' regarding the festivals: the essence of the day — meaning from the time the stars emerge until they emerge [again] on the night of the morrow — to exclude the addition which they derived to add from the profane onto the holy. And they expound (Sifrei Deuteronomy 32:48) regarding Noah and the Exodus and Moses — 'the essence of the day' — at midday, as is in the Sifrei, and Rashi wrote it in the section of Ha'azinu (Deuteronomy 32:48)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The reference to Terumot 7:1 concerns the halakhic term קֶרֶן (principal), literally 'horn,' used for repayment of the principal sum without the added fifth; Ramban connects this to the Aramaic קַרְנָא as 'body/essence.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:59:11.443132723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}